# Procedural Generation Rules

- **Deterministic**: Use seeds for all procedural content; same seed must produce the same result (reproducible saves, tests).
- **Chunk-based**: Generate world in chunks, not the entire world at once; load/unload or stream as needed.
- **Separation**: Keep generation logic separate from rendering; e.g. generate mesh data then hand to Unity mesh/rendering.
- **Pipeline**: Seed → noise/params → height/biome/mesh → LOD/collider; see `memory-bank/systemPatterns.md` (Procedural Generation Pipeline).
